description:
Lines 216-218 validate that user_profile.id contains no null bytes:
  if result.user_profile.id.contains('\0') {
    return Err(AuthError::WhoIsFailed('null byte in user_id'.into()));
  }

The check is defensive but the comment doesn't explain WHY null bytes are dangerous. A new contributor might think it's over-engineering or not know when to apply the same pattern.

SUGGESTION: Add comment explaining the threat model: 'Null bytes could break downstream string handling, logging, or filesystem operations — reject early at the trust boundary.'
